1. Primitive Data Types (Basic values)

These store single simple values.

✅ Example:
int a = 10;          // whole number
char ch = 'A';       // single character
boolean isTrue = true; // true/false

👉 These are not objects, just direct values.

🔹 2. Non-Primitive Data Structures (Complex / Collection of data)

These store multiple values or relationships.

📦 1. Array (Fixed size)
int[] arr = {10, 20, 30, 40};

System.out.println(arr[0]); // 10

👉 Stores multiple values of same type

📋 2. List (Dynamic size)
import java.util.ArrayList;

ArrayList<Integer> list = new ArrayList<>();
list.add(10);
list.add(20);
list.add(20); // duplicates allowed

System.out.println(list); // [10, 20, 20]

👉 Ordered + duplicates allowed

📚 3. Stack (LIFO – Last In First Out)
import java.util.Stack;

Stack<Integer> stack = new Stack<>();
stack.push(10);
stack.push(20);

System.out.println(stack.pop()); // 20

👉 Like plate stack

🚶 4. Queue (FIFO – First In First Out)
import java.util.LinkedList;
import java.util.Queue;

Queue<Integer> queue = new LinkedList<>();
queue.add(10);
queue.add(20);

System.out.println(queue.poll()); // 10

👉 Like line in ticket counter

🔑 5. Map (Key → Value pair)
import java.util.HashMap;

HashMap<Integer, String> map = new HashMap<>();
map.put(1, "Apple");
map.put(2, "Banana");

System.out.println(map.get(1)); // Apple

👉 Like dictionary / phonebook

🌳 6. Tree (Hierarchical structure)
class Node {
    int data;
    Node left, right;

    Node(int data) {
        this.data = data;
    }
}

👉 Example structure:

      10
     /  \
    5    15

👉 Used in:

File system
Hierarchy data
🌐 7. Graph (Network structure)
import java.util.*;

class GraphExample {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Map<Integer, List<Integer>> graph = new HashMap<>();

        graph.put(1, Arrays.asList(2, 3));
        graph.put(2, Arrays.asList(1, 4));
        graph.put(3, Arrays.asList(1));
        graph.put(4, Arrays.asList(2));

        System.out.println(graph);
    }
}

👉 Example:

1 ---- 2
|      |
3      4

👉 Used in:

Google Maps
Social networks
